[00:25.29] I'd seen the bloodlands of Antietam
[00:31.58] The shotgun shack in Tupelo
[00:36.98] But a brick circumference left hollow by Sherman
[00:44.15] Crumbling before me how it moaned
[00:49.60] His shape swallows my recollection
[00:56.83] That phantom silhouette implied
[01:03.14] Strange fruit rotting from an airborne and hotter than hell
[01:09.46] Is this the king's last man I've spied?
[01:15.79] I stood there beside my companion
[01:22.18] Scratching a rumor he had heard
[01:28.40] Do you have a gun?
[01:29.39] What? He said, yeah, you mean this one?
[01:34.76] Straight down the barrel was his word
[01:40.14] And I smelt the fumes he inhaled swiftly
[01:47.39] Each word was hinged upon his choke
[01:53.69] Like kudzu creeping up a state tree discretely
[01:59.93] Forever bending as it broke
[02:06.30] And I heard the jangling keys of Graceland
[02:12.66] Ring from his teeth stained brown from coke
[02:19.00] Drunk and stumbling like a man of distinction
[02:25.27] They clamored shaking as he spoke
[02:31.59] Of droves of pilgrims at his doorway
[02:37.84] Of Reagan, Carter, Clinton, Gore
[02:44.10] Fortunes offered them, refused routinely
[02:50.51] This ain't no damn auction house he swore
[02:56.89] Black male standing around 6 foot something
[03:03.11] Ebbs through the waves of small town blight
[03:09.42] A minute coldly from southern affection
[03:15.70] Collides secretly into night
[03:21.13] Forgive those who trespass against us
[03:28.45] Began as the dead intruders plea
[03:34.70] Into the very muzzle I'd once peered into
[03:41.02] He gives the last words he will speak
[03:47.32] But that broken glass supports forced entry
[03:52.75] Reminds his lawyer through the phone
[03:59.12] What southern judge do you know, comforting gently
[04:05.46] Who jails white men who defend their home
[04:11.70] No souls were present for the moment
[04:18.09] His bombed out brick walls finally fell
[04:25.26] Lying face down in the throes of atonement
[04:30.68] Checked out of the Heartbreak Hotel
[04:37.00] 
[05:14.90] He was the uncast shadow of a southern myth
